ype":"p","text":"By the end of B.Tech/B.E., the student should be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Explain paint and coating chemistry."},{"text":"Understand pigments, binders, solvents and additives."},{"text":"Select appropriate resin systems for applications."},{"text":"Formulate basic paint systems."},{"text":"Understand pigment dispersion and grinding."},{"text":"Analyse rheological behaviour."},{"text":"Understand surface wetting and adhesion."},{"text":"Perform colour measurement and matching."},{"text":"Understand coating application methods."},{"text":"Perform basic coating-performance tests."},{"text":"Understand corrosion-protection coatings."},{"text":"Understand powder and water-based coating systems."},{"text":"Understand film formation and curing."},{"text":"Apply statistics and DOE to formulation development."},{"text":"Troubleshoot common paint defects."},{"text":"Understand laboratory and pilot-scale formulation."},{"text":"Support production scale-up."},{"text":"Use Excel and Python for formulation and quality analysis."},{"text":"Understand sustainable and low-VOC coating technologies."},{"text":"Document formulations, experiments and test results professionally."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal Portfolio"},{"type":"flow","items":["A strong portfolio should demonstrate formulation","testing","optimization","application"]},{"type":"h","text":"1. Water-Based Paint Formulation"},{"type":"p","text":"Measure:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Viscosity"},{"text":"Solids"},{"text":"Colour"},{"text":"Gloss"},{"text":"Adhesion"},{"text":"Drying"},{"text":"Water resistance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Anti-Corrosion Coating"},{"type":"p","text":"Evaluate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Adhesion"},{"text":"Salt-spray behaviour"},{"text":"Corrosion resistance"},{"text":"Film thickness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Colour Matching System"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a database of pigment formulations and develop an ML-assisted colour prediction model."},{"type":"h","text":"4. Paint Rheology Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse how:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Resin"},{"text":"Pigment"},{"text":"Solids"},{"text":"Additives"},{"text":"affect flow and application."}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Sustainable Paint"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop a:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Water-based"},{"text":"Bio-based"},{"text":"Low-VOC"},{"text":"Powder"},{"text":"coating and compare performance."}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Paint Defect Detection"},{"type":"p","text":"Use computer vision to identify surface defects from coated panels."},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"“A paint and coating technology professional specializing in polymer and resin chemistry, pigment dispersion, formulation, rheology, surface science, coating application and performance testing, with the ability to develop, optimize and scale sustainable high-performance paint systems for decorative, industrial and protective applications.”"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended progression"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Tech/B.E. Sugar / Oil / Paint / Rubber Technology → Paint Technology Intern → Junior Paint Technologist → Paint Technologist → Senior Paint Technologist / Coating R&D Engineer → Principal Paint Technologist → Paint Technology Lead / R&D Manager"}]}]}